WEBVTT

00:51.384 --> 00:52.761
The leaves are falling!

00:53.261 --> 00:55.972
Gosh, look at the leaves.

01:00.560 --> 01:01.770
You look good.

01:02.979 --> 01:04.022
Let's go.

01:10.070 --> 01:12.322
Seoul's current temperature is 21°C.

01:12.405 --> 01:14.824
The relative humidity is 43 percent.

01:14.908 --> 01:16.159
What was that?

01:17.118 --> 01:19.204
The high temperature and humidity

01:19.287 --> 01:21.623
of the North Pacific air mass
have retreated.

01:21.706 --> 01:26.086
The pleasant fall weather
that is neither hot nor cold has begun.

01:29.589 --> 01:32.550
There is a migratory anticyclone
from the west around this season,

01:32.634 --> 01:33.635
and it feels pleasant.

01:33.718 --> 01:34.844
I'll be back.

01:34.928 --> 01:38.807
Everything is wonderful
during this season, but I…

01:52.821 --> 01:54.239
got my heart broken.

04:05.119 --> 04:06.871
I never gave her anything.

04:12.543 --> 04:15.421
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

04:29.394 --> 04:30.436
Hello?

04:30.520 --> 04:32.021
Hey, it's me.

04:33.231 --> 04:35.942
Are you still using these lotion bottles?

04:36.025 --> 04:39.028
Yes, I haven't finished using them yet.

04:40.071 --> 04:41.823
Really? Okay.

04:46.911 --> 04:48.204
Also…

04:48.288 --> 04:51.624
are all these chargers yours?

04:51.708 --> 04:55.461
No, the black Type-C one is
Senior Forecaster Um's.

04:59.799 --> 05:01.884
There are several black ones.

05:02.468 --> 05:04.679
I'll pack them all up.
You can give it to him.

05:04.762 --> 05:05.972
Okay.

05:07.807 --> 05:08.850
By the way,

05:08.933 --> 05:12.729
you don't have to pack my things for me.

05:13.646 --> 05:14.772
I'll go later--

05:14.856 --> 05:18.109
It's okay. I'm almost done.
I'll hand them over at work.

05:18.693 --> 05:20.528
But they're heavy.

05:20.611 --> 05:22.613
- I'll stop by later--
- You don't need to.

05:22.697 --> 05:23.823
Bye.

06:11.788 --> 06:17.085
EPISODE 14
MIGRATORY ANTICYCLONE

06:51.410 --> 06:53.121
Director Jin!

07:03.798 --> 07:07.093
Are you here for your stuff?
I said I'd bring it to you. Wait here.

07:07.176 --> 07:08.928
There's a problem.

07:09.512 --> 07:10.555
What problem?

07:10.638 --> 07:12.807
They found out.

07:13.850 --> 07:14.934
Found out what?

07:15.017 --> 07:16.644
That we dated.

07:17.728 --> 07:18.813
What?

07:22.900 --> 07:25.695
I heard you're dating Director Jin.

07:26.904 --> 07:27.822
What?

07:27.905 --> 07:29.866
Were you already dating
when we stayed at her place?

07:30.908 --> 07:33.786
Where did you hear that from?

07:33.870 --> 07:35.455
It wasn't from anyone specific.

07:35.538 --> 07:37.790
Everyone on our team knew except me.

07:38.666 --> 07:40.418
Everyone?

07:40.501 --> 07:41.711
Everyone.

07:42.587 --> 07:44.297
Everyone on our team found out

07:45.006 --> 07:47.216
that you and I dated.

07:47.300 --> 07:49.260
What are you saying?

07:49.343 --> 07:51.512
They know that we went out?

07:51.596 --> 07:53.347
Yes. And I'm sure

07:53.431 --> 07:55.391
everyone in the KMA also knows by now.

07:55.475 --> 07:56.350
What?

07:57.351 --> 07:58.394
You scared me.

08:03.774 --> 08:06.486
I knew it.

08:06.569 --> 08:08.029
Why are you here?

08:08.112 --> 08:10.948
So that means you two dated at work.
Is that right?

08:11.032 --> 08:15.161
- Mom, that's--
- I knew there was something going on.

08:17.872 --> 08:20.249
- It's a misunderstanding.
- Misunderstanding, my foot.

08:21.167 --> 08:23.211
I knew you'd deny it.

08:23.294 --> 08:25.963
So I got evidence.

08:32.178 --> 08:33.221
Will you deny it?

08:33.846 --> 08:35.389
Will you still deny it?

09:09.799 --> 09:13.386
FATHER

09:22.061 --> 09:23.980
What do his parents do?

09:24.897 --> 09:26.065
Don't ask anything.

09:28.234 --> 09:30.194
I can ask that much.

09:31.070 --> 09:32.697
There's no point.

09:32.780 --> 09:33.906
Why not?

09:35.366 --> 09:37.451
We broke up.

09:37.535 --> 09:38.661
What's wrong?

09:38.744 --> 09:40.371
Are you just saying that

09:40.454 --> 09:42.748
- in case I ruin everything?
- Mom.

09:42.832 --> 09:43.874
Grade Eight or Nine?

09:43.958 --> 09:45.501
Can you please…

09:46.002 --> 09:48.754
This is important.

09:49.380 --> 09:53.009
It does slightly bother me
that he's your subordinate.

09:53.092 --> 09:54.802
But he's younger than you,

09:54.885 --> 09:57.346
so we should be more understanding.

09:58.139 --> 09:59.390
Did he go to university?

09:59.473 --> 10:01.058
Are both of his parents alive?

10:01.142 --> 10:02.810
Where do they live?

10:02.893 --> 10:04.270
I said we broke up.

10:04.854 --> 10:06.230
I ought to know

10:06.314 --> 10:08.649
about his parents
to have a better understanding

10:08.733 --> 10:10.401
of what kind of person he is.

10:10.484 --> 10:12.236
Then I won't make any mistakes

10:12.320 --> 10:14.572
when I eventually meet them.

10:14.655 --> 10:16.699
You're wrong, Mom. We broke up.

10:17.575 --> 10:18.576
I believed what you said

10:18.659 --> 10:20.661
and was arrogant,
thinking I was a great catch.

10:20.745 --> 10:22.413
Then he dumped me. Happy?

10:22.496 --> 10:24.457
I won't fall for it.

10:25.291 --> 10:27.752
Tell me his birthdate
and the time of his birth.

10:27.835 --> 10:28.669
Mom.

10:30.004 --> 10:32.590
What? Shouldn't you find out
about your compatibility?

10:32.673 --> 10:34.634
I can't believe this.

10:36.510 --> 10:38.429
Why don't you listen?

10:38.929 --> 10:43.684
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

11:11.128 --> 11:12.338
Are you okay?

11:16.967 --> 11:19.095
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

11:21.847 --> 11:24.475
Did you speak with your mother?

11:24.558 --> 11:25.476
FATHER

11:32.775 --> 11:35.152
The person you are calling
is currently unavailable…

11:35.236 --> 11:37.863
Come on. Why isn't he picking up?

11:37.947 --> 11:39.198
Tell me what happened.

11:39.281 --> 11:42.910
Okay. I was driving on the inside lane.

11:42.993 --> 11:44.245
I wasn't even speeding.

11:44.328 --> 11:47.289
But then, he suddenly walked
toward my car.

11:47.373 --> 11:49.041
I had no way to dodge him.

11:49.125 --> 11:52.044
- Is he serious?
- I'm truly innocent.

11:53.045 --> 11:55.339
Don't you lie through your teeth.

11:55.423 --> 11:57.716
You drove into me

11:57.800 --> 12:00.010
when I was just walking by!

12:00.094 --> 12:02.304
My head is split open!

12:02.388 --> 12:04.014
- I--
- You did nothing wrong?

12:07.601 --> 12:08.811
Damn it.

12:28.539 --> 12:31.375
Hey. Breakfast is ready.
Get dressed and come out.

12:32.376 --> 12:34.378
I'm not that hungry.

12:34.462 --> 12:36.338
But I made dumpling soup, your favorite.

12:36.422 --> 12:38.048
Look. Doesn't it look good?

12:40.342 --> 12:41.385
Sorry.

12:41.469 --> 12:43.679
I'm feeling nauseous right now.

12:44.472 --> 12:45.431
Okay.

12:59.945 --> 13:01.030
Yu-jin.

13:01.864 --> 13:03.032
Yes?

13:04.408 --> 13:06.118
If it's too much for you,

13:06.202 --> 13:09.830
let's postpone registering our marriage.

13:11.707 --> 13:13.751
I'm really fine,

13:13.834 --> 13:16.128
so you can take your time.

13:24.970 --> 13:27.723
Honestly, there are many things
I still don't know

13:27.806 --> 13:30.851
since this is my first time
getting married.

13:30.935 --> 13:33.062
I really wanted to do well,

13:33.145 --> 13:35.147
but nothing went the way I wanted.

13:35.231 --> 13:38.609
That's why I haven't been
a great husband to you.

13:39.235 --> 13:40.778
I was embarrassed,

13:41.570 --> 13:44.782
so I wanted to look tougher
in front of you.

13:47.785 --> 13:48.953
But…

13:49.745 --> 13:52.289
I'll put in more effort from now on.

13:58.921 --> 14:00.297
Let's make this work.

14:01.173 --> 14:02.299
Okay?

14:03.509 --> 14:04.552
Ki-jun.

14:11.350 --> 14:15.020
Don't go to work on an empty stomach.
How about some hot milk?

14:15.896 --> 14:16.939
Sure.

14:17.022 --> 14:19.275
Okay. Get ready and come out.

16:06.256 --> 16:08.175
Twelfth floor.

16:12.763 --> 16:13.931
Tae-kyung.

16:14.598 --> 16:16.016
Ha-kyung.

16:20.396 --> 16:22.439
I'm here because…

16:23.273 --> 16:24.984
- I'm--
- Mom sent you, right?

16:25.067 --> 16:25.901
What?

16:26.735 --> 16:28.278
Unbelievable.

16:30.406 --> 16:31.699
Doors closing.

16:32.783 --> 16:34.201
Doors opening.

16:34.785 --> 16:36.996
Hey, try to understand her.

16:37.079 --> 16:39.665
Imagine how worried sick
she was to send me here.

16:39.748 --> 16:43.419
Still, she shouldn't have sent you here
so early in the morning.

16:43.502 --> 16:46.714
You're right. I didn't know
you went to work this early.

16:46.797 --> 16:48.799
I didn't think I was too early.

16:48.882 --> 16:51.301
Why is she so obsessed with me

16:51.385 --> 16:53.137
and marrying me off?

16:53.220 --> 16:55.597
Why can't she believe that we broke up?

16:55.681 --> 16:57.391
You broke up? With whom?

16:58.559 --> 16:59.560
Whatever.

17:00.060 --> 17:02.146
Tell her to mind her own business.

17:02.229 --> 17:03.480
Never mind. I'll tell her.

17:04.064 --> 17:05.607
Hey! No.

17:05.691 --> 17:07.192
She'll kill me.

17:07.776 --> 17:09.862
Why would she? You did nothing wrong.

17:09.945 --> 17:10.821
What?

17:12.031 --> 17:15.367
Do you think you'll be nice
if you talk to her right now?

17:15.451 --> 17:18.579
You'll talk harshly and upset her.

17:18.662 --> 17:21.123
Then whom will she vent at? It'll be me.

17:21.206 --> 17:24.168
She'll vent at me for days on end.

17:24.752 --> 17:27.296
Gosh. Hey, Ha-kyung.

17:27.379 --> 17:30.674
Are you seriously going
to subject me to that?

17:30.758 --> 17:33.844
That's exactly why you shouldn't call her.

17:33.927 --> 17:34.970
I oppose it.

17:35.054 --> 17:36.764
Never. At all costs.

17:40.142 --> 17:41.852
Fine. What would you know?

17:43.854 --> 17:45.314
Thank you, my dear sister.

17:49.943 --> 17:51.653
You're really admirable.

17:53.072 --> 17:55.282
You didn't see me today. Go to work.

17:56.950 --> 17:58.368
I'll go first. Bye.

18:09.797 --> 18:10.881
Honey.

18:12.049 --> 18:13.342
Look at this.

18:15.719 --> 18:17.012
What is that?

18:19.014 --> 18:20.808
Check this out.

18:23.602 --> 18:24.978
My dear Bo-mi.

18:25.062 --> 18:26.063
Happy birthday!

18:27.272 --> 18:28.357
Isn't it funny?

18:29.942 --> 18:32.319
An alarm goes off for self-protection.

18:32.402 --> 18:35.864
She'll love to hang this
on her bag as a keychain, right?

18:37.491 --> 18:38.909
She's in seventh grade.

18:38.992 --> 18:40.702
Of course. I know that.

18:40.786 --> 18:43.413
What kind of a seventh-grader
would want that?

18:45.999 --> 18:48.001
Really? This is a brand new toy.

18:48.085 --> 18:49.419
Unbelievable.

18:50.003 --> 18:51.630
I'm going to school.

18:51.713 --> 18:53.132
Eat first.

18:53.715 --> 18:55.425
No, thanks. I have a stomachache.

18:56.135 --> 18:57.302
Why is she sick?

18:57.386 --> 18:58.595
It's that time of the month.

18:59.680 --> 19:02.349
- That time?
- Bo-mi, at least drink this.

19:03.308 --> 19:04.393
What time?

19:08.772 --> 19:10.482
Oh, that time…

19:16.071 --> 19:18.323
KOREA METEOROLOGICAL ADMINISTRATION

19:20.534 --> 19:21.994
- Seriously?
- Yes.

19:22.077 --> 19:24.079
- Since when?
- I heard they're dating.

19:24.163 --> 19:26.248
- Another colleague?
- How long has it been?

19:26.331 --> 19:27.666
I heard it's Director Jin of Team Two.

19:28.500 --> 19:30.836
I HEARD THEY'RE DATING

19:30.919 --> 19:32.254
ANOTHER COLLEAGUE?

19:33.255 --> 19:34.798
HOW LONG HAS IT BEEN?

19:34.882 --> 19:36.341
REALLY?
I HEARD HE'S WITH DIRECTOR JIN

19:36.425 --> 19:37.593
THEY LOOK GOOD TOGETHER

19:37.676 --> 19:43.056
THEY'RE GOING OUT

19:43.140 --> 19:44.558
THEY ARE?
THEY'RE REALLY DATING?

19:44.641 --> 19:46.351
REALLY? ANOTHER COLLEAGUE?

19:48.770 --> 19:51.023
- Goodbye.
- Goodbye.

20:04.203 --> 20:05.579
I heard they're dating.

20:05.662 --> 20:06.914
Since when?

20:06.997 --> 20:08.248
They look good together.

20:10.459 --> 20:11.627
Is it true?

20:12.836 --> 20:15.505
- Forecaster Lee?
- And Director Jin?

20:15.589 --> 20:17.049
Are you serious?

20:19.343 --> 20:21.053
Will she get married this time?

20:21.136 --> 20:23.138
They suit each other.
What a lovely couple.

20:47.955 --> 20:50.082
What's done is done.

20:50.749 --> 20:52.292
There's no turning back.

20:52.876 --> 20:53.877
Sorry?

20:55.254 --> 20:57.422
I'm talking about Director Jin here.

20:58.215 --> 21:00.217
She's already experienced the pain

21:00.300 --> 21:02.844
of dating a colleague.

21:03.887 --> 21:07.474
Yet you still decided to date her.
What choice do you have?

21:07.557 --> 21:10.602
"Heavy is the head that wears the crown."

21:11.186 --> 21:13.814
- Don't you agree?
- Right.

21:15.565 --> 21:18.151
But to tell you the truth--

21:18.235 --> 21:21.613
It's okay. I root for you guys.

21:22.489 --> 21:24.992
I hope you have a beautiful relationship

21:25.492 --> 21:30.414
and I also hope
she doesn't get hurt again.

21:31.248 --> 21:34.126
If she gets hurt in the same way again,

21:34.209 --> 21:38.213
she might really get on
a flight to Geneva.

21:39.214 --> 21:41.842
I'm not just saying this for her sake.

21:41.925 --> 21:43.218
Don't you think having

21:43.302 --> 21:47.139
three different directors
in a year is ridiculous?

21:48.307 --> 21:51.393
We're finally starting
to build up teamwork.

21:51.935 --> 21:52.936
Right.

21:53.645 --> 21:54.896
But then again,

21:55.439 --> 21:58.692
I'm sure you guys thought long
and hard before making this decision.

21:59.526 --> 22:03.363
I doubt you guys
would have dated to begin with

22:04.406 --> 22:05.991
if it wasn't serious.

22:06.533 --> 22:07.701
Right.

22:10.037 --> 22:12.205
Don't mind the others.

22:13.623 --> 22:14.833
- Okay?
- Okay.

22:14.916 --> 22:17.252
- Good luck, Forecaster Lee.
- Thank you.

22:46.031 --> 22:47.365
What is it?

22:49.242 --> 22:50.410
What should we do?

22:50.494 --> 22:54.247
People are taking it
more seriously than they should.

22:54.331 --> 22:55.499
Ignore them.

22:55.582 --> 22:58.001
Don't listen to them or reply.

22:58.585 --> 23:01.213
Then they'll stop talking
about it over time.

23:02.255 --> 23:04.758
- But--
- I'm hanging up if it isn't about work.

23:05.258 --> 23:07.886
And don't call me
about things like this at work.

23:33.036 --> 23:34.162
Good work.

23:34.246 --> 23:35.413
Thank you.

23:44.881 --> 23:46.591
- Thank you.
- Sure.

23:47.342 --> 23:48.885
Anything in particular?

23:49.594 --> 23:51.096
Things are peaceful for once.

23:54.349 --> 23:57.394
The upper-level trough
near Lake Baikal is developing

23:57.477 --> 23:58.937
quicker than it did last year.

23:59.020 --> 24:01.106
It's only a week faster.

24:01.189 --> 24:02.983
In any case, the weather's nice.

24:03.775 --> 24:06.444
The disaster prevention season is over,
so we have more time now.

24:06.528 --> 24:08.655
It's the best season to fall in love.

24:11.658 --> 24:13.785
It's the best season to do many things.

24:14.369 --> 24:16.913
I think the live monitoring team
won't be too busy.

24:16.997 --> 24:20.375
To prepare for the winter season,
why don't you analyze the first frost

24:20.458 --> 24:22.252
in the past 30 years?

24:22.335 --> 24:24.546
Isn't it too soon?

24:25.338 --> 24:26.506
Come on.

24:26.590 --> 24:29.050
We're finally taking a breather.
Let us relax.

24:29.134 --> 24:32.012
The prevention season may be over,
but you should still be alert.

24:33.430 --> 24:36.141
Migratory anticyclones are always
followed by cyclones.

24:36.224 --> 24:37.976
The slightest change in the air current

24:38.059 --> 24:40.478
causes abnormal weather,
so let's be on our toes.

24:40.562 --> 24:43.690
We don't have time to joke around at work.

24:45.108 --> 24:46.860
All right.

24:47.444 --> 24:49.112
It was just one joke.

24:49.613 --> 24:52.657
You don't have to make
such a big deal out of it.

25:36.952 --> 25:38.119
Goodness.

25:43.875 --> 25:46.211
Are you coming in or going out?

25:46.294 --> 25:47.462
Well…

25:48.255 --> 25:49.673
You know Mi-seon, right?

25:49.756 --> 25:51.091
We went to the same college.

25:51.174 --> 25:53.510
She had a publication party yesterday,

25:53.593 --> 25:55.470
and I was meaning to have just one drink.

25:56.096 --> 25:57.555
She published another book?

25:57.639 --> 25:58.932
Yes.

25:59.015 --> 26:00.809
Good going.

26:01.393 --> 26:05.105
It's been less than a year
since she last published a book.

26:05.188 --> 26:07.232
How many years has it been for you?

26:08.024 --> 26:09.401
I'm publishing one too.

26:09.484 --> 26:11.528
That's why I signed
a contract with a publisher.

26:11.611 --> 26:15.073
Goodness. We'll see
if you really publish one or not.

26:15.156 --> 26:19.327
Who knows how long it'll take
when you're wasting your time like this?

26:19.411 --> 26:21.329
Jeez. Mom.

26:21.413 --> 26:23.290
What if mine becomes a bestseller?

26:23.373 --> 26:26.126
Can we please talk about that
after you publish one,

26:26.209 --> 26:27.669
Writer Jin?

26:27.752 --> 26:28.628
Please?

26:29.212 --> 26:32.007
Goodness.
What's the point of having two kids?

26:32.090 --> 26:35.218
Neither of them understands me.

26:35.302 --> 26:38.096
It's about time you let Ha-kyung be.

26:38.179 --> 26:41.474
Who cares if she's dating someone
or is against marriage?

26:41.558 --> 26:43.268
Did she deny it in front of you too?

26:43.351 --> 26:44.352
Deny what?

26:44.436 --> 26:46.771
That she's dating her colleague.

26:46.855 --> 26:48.064
Her colleague?

26:48.148 --> 26:50.775
She's dating her colleague? Who?

26:51.359 --> 26:52.610
You know…

26:52.694 --> 26:55.613
That handsomely tall guy with a pale face.

26:55.697 --> 26:57.532
The very good-looking one.

26:58.241 --> 27:00.702
Handsomely tall and looks like an actor?

27:00.785 --> 27:01.828
Mr. Shin Seok-ho?

27:01.911 --> 27:03.413
Who is that?

27:03.496 --> 27:06.750
The guy who lives above her.
They're on the same team.

27:06.833 --> 27:08.168
Come on.

27:08.835 --> 27:11.421
He's neither handsomely tall

27:11.504 --> 27:13.715
nor extremely good-looking.

27:13.798 --> 27:15.216
He's handsome enough.

27:17.635 --> 27:21.139
Keep talking. Who's the guy?

27:21.222 --> 27:22.807
His name is Lee Si-woo.

27:23.808 --> 27:27.645
You know, they were living together
until not long ago.

27:28.229 --> 27:30.982
They're secretly dating
behind their colleagues' backs,

27:31.066 --> 27:33.693
but she's vehemently denying it
in front of me.

27:33.777 --> 27:35.195
Of course, she would.

27:35.278 --> 27:37.280
If not, you'd bombard her with questions.

27:37.364 --> 27:38.573
Such as?

27:38.656 --> 27:41.284
"Who are his parents?
What does his father do?"

27:41.368 --> 27:44.079
"Which university did he attend?
Grade Eight or Nine?"

27:44.162 --> 27:46.539
"Tell me his birthdate
and the time of his birth."

27:46.623 --> 27:49.959
Did she tell you
that I asked those questions?

27:50.960 --> 27:52.670
She doesn't have to tell me that.

27:52.754 --> 27:54.756
Everyone knows
about the questions you ask.

27:54.839 --> 27:56.925
Don't exaggerate.

27:57.425 --> 28:00.804
Mom, just turn a blind eye to them.

28:00.887 --> 28:02.555
If you interfere,

28:02.639 --> 28:04.766
you'll just ruin what they already have.

28:05.600 --> 28:08.269
Ha-kyung is seeing someone again.

28:08.353 --> 28:10.438
Be satisfied with that, will you?

28:10.522 --> 28:12.649
That's enough. Fine.

28:14.150 --> 28:15.318
I got it.

28:17.862 --> 28:19.656
- Wait.
- What?

28:19.739 --> 28:21.074
Where did you sleep again?

28:21.157 --> 28:22.534
At Shin…

28:24.661 --> 28:27.163
- At Ms. Shin's.
- But you said Mi-seon earlier.

28:27.747 --> 28:31.584
She and I attended
Mi-seon's publication party together.

28:32.293 --> 28:34.170
I already told you this!

28:47.851 --> 28:50.478
Gosh, she's so intuitive.

28:59.028 --> 29:02.490
Why did you leave so early?
I was going to make you some coffee.

29:11.249 --> 29:14.419
Are you free later this evening?

29:20.425 --> 29:21.551
Sure.

29:23.511 --> 29:24.804
- Senior Forecaster Um.
- Yes?

29:24.888 --> 29:27.474
Here's the temperature change analysis
that you wanted yesterday.

29:27.557 --> 29:29.684
- Thanks. I'll check it out.
- Okay.

29:29.768 --> 29:30.852
By the way,

29:30.935 --> 29:32.479
how old are your kids again?

29:32.562 --> 29:34.522
The eldest is ten,
and the second one is eight.

29:34.606 --> 29:37.400
- Why?
- Then you wouldn't know.

29:37.484 --> 29:38.902
What? What do you mean?

29:39.611 --> 29:43.364
You see, Bo-mi's birthday
is just around the corner.

29:43.948 --> 29:47.702
But I have no idea what to get her.

29:47.786 --> 29:50.955
I see. What grade is she again?

29:51.039 --> 29:51.873
Seventh grade.

29:52.540 --> 29:53.750
Seventh grade.

29:53.833 --> 29:54.876
A luxury item.

29:55.627 --> 29:56.753
A luxury item?

29:56.836 --> 29:59.130
Don't be absurd. She's just a student.

29:59.214 --> 30:00.965
You guys are so behind.

30:01.049 --> 30:04.511
It's a trend these days for teenagers
to have at least one luxury item.

30:04.594 --> 30:07.388
Even my niece asked her mom
to buy her a luxury winter jacket

30:07.472 --> 30:10.308
in return for raising
her grades on a mock test.

30:10.391 --> 30:11.601
Seriously?

30:13.686 --> 30:15.730
How much would that cost?

30:15.814 --> 30:17.398
Jeez, I bet a hefty sum.

30:17.982 --> 30:18.983
- Right?
- Yes.

30:21.027 --> 30:22.278
That's…

30:23.988 --> 30:25.865
For a middle-schooler?

30:25.949 --> 30:27.992
That's insane.

30:28.743 --> 30:31.204
I've never even touched
such an expensive jacket before.

30:31.287 --> 30:32.705
That's…

30:33.706 --> 30:34.958
Soo-jin.

30:35.041 --> 30:37.710
Can you search up
migratory anticyclones' courses

30:37.794 --> 30:40.088
in the past decade
from late September to mid-October?

30:40.171 --> 30:42.590
Sorry? A decade's worth?

30:43.174 --> 30:44.384
Yes. All of it.

30:47.053 --> 30:48.054
Yes, ma'am.

30:50.890 --> 30:52.851
What should I do?

30:52.934 --> 30:55.144
Just buy her a decent gift.

30:55.228 --> 30:56.938
Luxury goods are too much for students.

30:57.522 --> 30:59.315
And they're extremely expensive.

31:00.149 --> 31:01.025
Do you think so?

31:01.109 --> 31:02.861
Do they really wear those?

31:04.362 --> 31:05.905
ASSISTANT DIRECTOR PARK SUNG-JIN

31:08.658 --> 31:10.368
Soo-jin, have you made up your mind?

31:14.163 --> 31:16.207
Assistant Director Im
took a leave of absence?

31:16.791 --> 31:17.625
Why?

31:17.709 --> 31:20.795
Her husband is moving to the US for work,
so she'll be away for a few years.

31:20.879 --> 31:21.963
I see.

31:22.046 --> 31:24.132
So we have a vacancy.

31:24.716 --> 31:25.592
Okay.

31:26.843 --> 31:30.513
Speaking of which, didn't you always want
to transfer to the Policy Division?

31:30.597 --> 31:31.681
I did.

31:31.764 --> 31:33.975
I even requested
a transfer numerous times.

31:34.058 --> 31:35.268
Give it another try.

31:35.977 --> 31:39.564
Knowing our director,
you'll be accepted in no time.

31:39.647 --> 31:40.940
- Really?
- Yes.

31:46.237 --> 31:48.573
SOO-JIN, HAVE YOU MADE UP YOUR MIND?

31:55.538 --> 31:58.666
Who's analyzing the prognostic chart
for the next 24 hours?

32:00.710 --> 32:01.836
It's me, ma'am.

32:07.634 --> 32:09.469
How long will it take?

32:10.386 --> 32:11.679
I'll finish it in an hour.

32:15.725 --> 32:19.479
I need the cut-off low development
on Lake Baikal as well.

32:19.562 --> 32:21.064
I'm also looking at it right now.

32:22.732 --> 32:25.985
I'll prepare the prognostic chart
as well for your convenience.

32:30.657 --> 32:32.241
It's okay. Just give me what you have.

32:32.825 --> 32:35.411
- It won't take long.
- Just give it to me.

32:35.495 --> 32:36.621
Yes, ma'am.

32:44.212 --> 32:46.130
Ignore them.

32:53.012 --> 32:55.181
Assistant Director Kim,
can you ask the NWP Team

32:55.264 --> 32:58.101
for the foreign models
for the next three months?

33:01.938 --> 33:02.981
Assistant Director Kim.

33:03.564 --> 33:06.234
Why is he so distracted?

33:11.948 --> 33:15.994
When did Director Jin
and Forecaster Lee fall in love?

33:16.077 --> 33:17.662
Misery sure loves company.

33:17.745 --> 33:21.457
He was the one Reporter Chae dated
before getting married.

33:21.541 --> 33:23.251
Hold on. What is it, then?

33:23.334 --> 33:25.586
- Crossed in love?
- Addicted to love.

33:25.670 --> 33:26.546
That's what you talk about?

33:28.464 --> 33:29.298
Sir.

33:30.800 --> 33:32.385
I'm sorry.

33:33.052 --> 33:35.430
I only read the messages.

33:39.726 --> 33:41.185
Ask the NWP Team

33:41.269 --> 33:44.480
for any extra information needed
for the next three months.

33:44.564 --> 33:45.565
Yes, sir.

33:56.367 --> 33:59.162
Do you think Deputy Director Han
and Reporter Chae know about this?

33:59.245 --> 34:00.913
I'm sure they heard the rumors.

34:00.997 --> 34:03.666
This is why
you should never date a colleague.

34:56.177 --> 34:58.596
About the climate projection report
for this winter…

34:59.263 --> 35:02.266
We need to add more
to the part about La Niña.

35:03.518 --> 35:05.978
I see. Is this because of
the statement from NOAA?

35:06.062 --> 35:07.522
That too.

35:08.189 --> 35:10.525
Europe, Japan,
and Australia's forecast centers

35:10.608 --> 35:12.860
also predicted La Niña.

35:13.486 --> 35:16.280
I need to send out
a news release by 4 p.m.,

35:16.364 --> 35:18.366
so please update it before then.

35:32.755 --> 35:34.006
Is that all?

35:37.009 --> 35:39.178
It seems like there's something else.

35:45.434 --> 35:46.727
I've known Ha-kyung

35:47.395 --> 35:49.814
for quite a long time.

35:49.897 --> 35:52.316
I must have gotten used to her

35:52.984 --> 35:57.029
because I forgot
how precious she was to me.

35:58.489 --> 36:00.700
I felt so entitled.

36:00.783 --> 36:04.287
And after some time,
I stopped feeling grateful

36:04.370 --> 36:06.581
and forgot how much she meant to me.

36:07.206 --> 36:09.083
What are you trying to say?

36:12.795 --> 36:15.506
At the end of things,
she just considered me an asshole.

36:18.092 --> 36:20.178
But you're different.

36:20.261 --> 36:22.597
You'll hurt her much more than I did.

36:28.603 --> 36:30.438
She dumped me.

36:30.521 --> 36:32.815
Do you think
the others would think the same?

36:34.650 --> 36:38.154
People don't care about breakups.

36:38.779 --> 36:40.615
They're just curious

36:41.657 --> 36:43.159
about the reason.

36:46.412 --> 36:47.830
At work…

36:48.623 --> 36:50.416
Especially if it's about dating,

36:51.083 --> 36:53.044
women tend to suffer more

36:53.127 --> 36:55.796
than we men do.

36:55.880 --> 36:58.257
People will gossip more about her than you

36:58.341 --> 37:00.551
because of her past with me.

37:00.635 --> 37:01.844
However…

37:02.970 --> 37:05.223
you and I both know

37:05.932 --> 37:09.518
that she deserves better
than to be a laughingstock.

37:10.102 --> 37:11.979
- I know.
- So…

37:15.524 --> 37:18.027
I know it may sound ridiculous,
coming from me.

37:19.362 --> 37:21.864
But I hope you think twice
before breaking up with her.

37:24.200 --> 37:27.995
But if you must break up,
I hope you'll be courteous.

37:30.206 --> 37:32.166
Don't be an asshole like me.

37:43.803 --> 37:46.430
The chill is moving southward
quicker than we expected.

37:46.514 --> 37:48.683
Let's hear what the analysts have to say.

37:48.766 --> 37:51.852
If this is the case, we'll have to inform
the Impact Forecast Team.

37:52.395 --> 37:53.354
Let's do that.

37:54.855 --> 37:56.190
A cold wave out of the blue?

37:56.274 --> 37:57.650
What's going on?

37:58.150 --> 38:02.029
The cold continental anticyclone
suddenly developed in Siberia

38:02.113 --> 38:03.656
and will impact our weather.

38:03.739 --> 38:06.784
You can see the chill going southward
through the satellite photos.

38:06.867 --> 38:10.246
The cold continental anticyclone
on Lake Baikal developed quicker

38:10.329 --> 38:13.666
since the North Pacific's anticyclone
was in the far east.

38:14.375 --> 38:16.335
This just adds insult to injury.

38:16.419 --> 38:17.753
How is Daegwallyeong?

38:17.837 --> 38:21.299
The morning temperature will be subzero
starting with the inland areas

38:21.382 --> 38:23.467
such as Daegwallyeong and Cheorwon.

38:23.551 --> 38:26.262
Assistant Director Shin,
what's the forecast for this week?

38:26.345 --> 38:29.098
We've sent out a notice
about the temperature dropping

38:29.181 --> 38:30.641
this weekend.

38:31.267 --> 38:33.352
If the temperature drops 10°C or more,

38:33.436 --> 38:35.313
the sensible temperature will be colder.

38:35.396 --> 38:37.398
You're right. This is not good.

38:40.109 --> 38:41.235
At this rate,

38:41.319 --> 38:43.654
all the farmers shipping
their goods will suffer.

38:44.280 --> 38:47.283
It's the kimchi season soon,
so the radishes on Ganghwa Island

38:47.366 --> 38:50.077
and the cabbages in Gangwon Province
will be damaged

38:50.661 --> 38:54.040
as well as the soybeans and chili peppers
in North Gyeongsang Province.

38:56.000 --> 38:57.501
Let's keep monitoring

38:57.585 --> 39:00.588
until the final analysis and decide on
the cold wave advisory in two days.

39:00.671 --> 39:02.465
And send out
an official paper on the cold wave

39:02.548 --> 39:04.508
to the farming organizations.

39:04.592 --> 39:05.968
We'll do our best,

39:06.052 --> 39:09.221
but if you knew that the anticyclone
was developing quicker this year,

39:09.930 --> 39:12.600
you should have informed us sooner.

39:13.392 --> 39:16.937
But then again, you must have been
too busy going on dates. Jeez.

39:20.566 --> 39:21.984
- Hey.
- Yes?

39:22.068 --> 39:24.111
How's your wife doing?

39:24.195 --> 39:26.238
- Good.
- That's good.

39:27.698 --> 39:30.743
His wife used to be my subordinate.

39:31.994 --> 39:33.412
That's right.

39:33.496 --> 39:37.416
They had one passionate relationship
at work, right?

39:37.500 --> 39:40.336
Jeez. One day,
they'd be all over each other.

39:40.419 --> 39:42.505
Another day,
they'd ruin the work atmosphere.

39:42.588 --> 39:44.799
You're right. We were all walking

39:44.882 --> 39:46.634
- on eggshells.
- That's right.

39:46.717 --> 39:49.887
I'll speak with the Office of Spokesperson
and send out that official paper

39:49.970 --> 39:51.847
as soon as possible.

39:53.766 --> 39:55.226
Please understand.

39:55.893 --> 39:57.520
He's going through male menopause.

39:57.603 --> 39:58.896
We'll take care of it.

40:01.982 --> 40:04.276
You didn't have to do that.

40:04.360 --> 40:06.612
They need to know
if they did something wrong.

40:06.695 --> 40:08.072
Otherwise, they'll keep talking.

40:09.865 --> 40:11.158
He's right.

40:11.242 --> 40:13.452
Work and personal life should be separate.

40:13.536 --> 40:16.330
He shouldn't have mentioned
you guys at work.

40:16.414 --> 40:18.040
I completely agree with you.

40:18.833 --> 40:20.000
Guys.

40:20.084 --> 40:21.877
A cold wave is coming.

40:22.461 --> 40:23.796
Let's get back to work.

40:23.879 --> 40:25.631
I have something to tell you.

40:28.509 --> 40:29.510
To be honest…

40:34.306 --> 40:36.142
Forecaster Lee and I--

40:36.225 --> 40:38.436
I hope you support us.

40:39.812 --> 40:42.690
We'll keep our work
and personal life separate.

40:43.983 --> 40:45.317
Right?

40:48.237 --> 40:49.405
Sure.

40:49.488 --> 40:51.073
You guys look nice.

40:52.366 --> 40:54.160
But don't make it too obvious.

40:54.785 --> 40:55.828
Okay, then.

41:15.931 --> 41:18.559
Why did you do that? What's the matter?

41:18.642 --> 41:21.896
Let's keep it a secret for the time being.

41:21.979 --> 41:24.273
- Keep what a secret?
- Our breakup.

41:24.356 --> 41:25.608
I don't understand.

41:27.026 --> 41:29.195
It's just too much of a hassle.

41:29.278 --> 41:31.697
They just found out that we were dating.

41:31.780 --> 41:33.532
Imagine if they found out we broke up.

41:33.616 --> 41:36.911
Those who like to talk
will be quick to assume.

41:36.994 --> 41:39.038
They will gossip among themselves.

41:39.622 --> 41:40.456
So…

41:40.998 --> 41:43.083
let's keep it a secret for the time being.

41:43.751 --> 41:44.960
Until the dust settles.

41:45.711 --> 41:46.795
Is this because of me?

41:49.757 --> 41:51.675
Are you worried people will think

41:51.759 --> 41:53.719
I got dumped again?

41:55.137 --> 41:56.263
No.

41:57.598 --> 42:00.601
Then? Is it because you feel bad for me?

42:00.684 --> 42:02.770
- No.
- Then what is it?

42:02.853 --> 42:04.355
I just don't want to hear them.

42:05.397 --> 42:06.774
They gossip

42:06.857 --> 42:08.526
when they know nothing about you.

42:08.609 --> 42:10.569
I can't stand that.

42:12.863 --> 42:13.989
That's why.

42:16.784 --> 42:19.787
Didn't you know?
That's the price of dating a colleague.

42:20.454 --> 42:22.831
People gossip about your relationship

42:22.915 --> 42:25.459
at all times even if
you break up or don't.

42:27.670 --> 42:29.338
Despite knowing that,

42:31.131 --> 42:33.592
I chose that path once again.

42:41.100 --> 42:42.768
- I'm sorry.
- Don't apologize.

42:43.394 --> 42:44.937
It was my choice.

42:45.020 --> 42:47.982
I chose to love and break up.

42:49.608 --> 42:51.110
So don't be sorry.

42:51.193 --> 42:55.072
It's me who needs
to bear with the consequences.

42:55.656 --> 42:57.324
It's unbearable for me.

43:00.744 --> 43:03.455
This breakup…

43:06.125 --> 43:07.334
is too painful for me.

43:09.837 --> 43:11.505
I didn't want to see you in pain

43:12.464 --> 43:14.300
because of this poor breakup.

43:15.050 --> 43:15.884
But…

43:17.886 --> 43:21.265
I didn't expect this
to cause you even more pain.

43:49.293 --> 43:50.461
Yu-jin.

43:52.004 --> 43:54.214
This is yours from today on.

43:54.882 --> 43:56.050
What?

43:56.967 --> 43:59.470
Isn't Se-hui in charge
of this special article?

44:00.387 --> 44:04.099
She wants less work
for the time being because she's pregnant.

44:04.683 --> 44:06.727
No way. She's pregnant?

44:09.271 --> 44:11.690
Being pregnant
doesn't entitle her to anything,

44:11.774 --> 44:14.151
but she was so brazen.

44:15.319 --> 44:17.363
That's understandable
during early pregnancy.

44:18.113 --> 44:20.908
In that case, she should've just gotten
a maternity leave.

44:20.991 --> 44:24.203
That way, I could ask
the company for more manpower.

44:24.286 --> 44:26.705
But right now,
I can't do anything about it.

44:27.331 --> 44:29.667
Until when am I in charge of this?

44:29.750 --> 44:31.210
Forever.

44:32.252 --> 44:33.212
What?

44:33.879 --> 44:36.548
Consider it yours from today on.

44:37.299 --> 44:40.719
Taking a leave for childbirth
and childrearing will mean

44:40.803 --> 44:43.263
she won't be working for a year or two.

44:43.806 --> 44:45.349
Once that happens,

44:45.432 --> 44:47.935
she will lose her edge.

44:48.018 --> 44:50.938
If she can't get on top of her game,
it'll be the end of her career.

44:52.106 --> 44:53.023
Come on.

44:53.649 --> 44:56.026
Her career wouldn't
come to an end because of that.

44:58.112 --> 44:59.988
What? Do you think I'm lying?

45:00.781 --> 45:02.324
Ask around then.

45:02.408 --> 45:05.411
Countless colleagues of yours gave birth

45:05.494 --> 45:07.162
and lost their jobs.

45:08.664 --> 45:12.501
Consider this
your golden opportunity and do well.

45:13.085 --> 45:15.337
You've always wanted your own column.

45:16.004 --> 45:17.423
You do know

45:17.506 --> 45:20.676
that the column is published
on the society front page, right?

45:23.429 --> 45:24.471
Right.

45:25.264 --> 45:26.348
I understand.

45:27.850 --> 45:29.685
Okay. Goodbye.

45:46.827 --> 45:49.913
What are you pondering so hard about?
You look gorgeous.

45:51.582 --> 45:52.624
It's nothing.

45:54.084 --> 45:56.628
What's wrong? Did something happen?

45:59.423 --> 46:02.342
Actually, I'm in charge of a column now.

46:02.426 --> 46:03.427
Seriously?

46:03.510 --> 46:05.929
You got your own column?

46:07.181 --> 46:10.100
Come on. That's great news.

46:10.184 --> 46:11.435
Hold on.

46:11.518 --> 46:14.271
I'm done for the day
once the briefing is over.

46:14.354 --> 46:16.315
How about we have some wine?

46:16.899 --> 46:18.233
I can't drink.

46:18.317 --> 46:21.111
What's wrong?
Are you still feeling unwell?

46:24.114 --> 46:26.241
What's wrong? Tell me.

46:26.325 --> 46:27.826
I'm here for you. Okay?

46:28.785 --> 46:30.579
Do you need a new laptop?

46:30.662 --> 46:32.831
Or a handbag? Should we go shopping?

46:34.625 --> 46:35.792
I'm…

46:36.376 --> 46:37.753
pregnant.

46:45.177 --> 46:46.178
What?

46:47.179 --> 46:48.889
I'm 12 weeks pregnant.

46:57.189 --> 47:00.692
Good work, everyone. Let's go home now.

47:00.776 --> 47:01.777
Yes, sir.

47:02.402 --> 47:04.655
All right.

47:44.528 --> 47:46.655
Assistant Director Shin,
do you have plans today?

47:46.738 --> 47:49.324
Sorry? Yes, I do.

47:49.408 --> 47:51.702
You're playing a new game, aren't you?

47:51.785 --> 47:54.496
- You're wrong.
- Then what is it?

47:55.122 --> 47:57.291
Are you going
on a blind date or something?

47:58.500 --> 48:00.711
- No, I'm not.
- He denied it.

48:01.336 --> 48:02.254
He denied it.

48:07.134 --> 48:08.260
Hello.

48:14.016 --> 48:15.726
You came in last.

48:17.519 --> 48:18.562
No.

48:19.146 --> 48:21.898
I have a very important appointment today.

48:21.982 --> 48:24.151
Goodness.

48:25.152 --> 48:26.445
You can go down first.

48:29.156 --> 48:30.365
Excuse me.

48:45.547 --> 48:46.840
This is awkward.

48:47.507 --> 48:49.009
It's fine for me.

48:50.636 --> 48:54.514
So how long do we need to keep this up?

48:54.598 --> 48:55.891
Until the others

48:56.683 --> 48:58.685
stop talking about us.

49:05.442 --> 49:07.110
Do we have to do this?

49:07.194 --> 49:08.236
Yes.

49:08.987 --> 49:10.030
I'd like us to.

49:24.961 --> 49:26.838
HAN KI-JUN

49:35.055 --> 49:36.848
CHAE YU-JIN

49:49.945 --> 49:51.238
Welcome.

50:39.411 --> 50:41.747
I thought there would be a traffic jam…

50:41.830 --> 50:45.625
I see. You took the subway
to avoid traffic

50:45.709 --> 50:47.753
but you got the exits mixed up.

50:54.050 --> 50:55.844
Where should we go?

51:07.272 --> 51:08.565
Oh, no!

51:08.648 --> 51:09.775
Hold on.

51:09.858 --> 51:11.526
- I'm sorry. Oh, no.
- What is this?

51:11.610 --> 51:13.570
- Oh, no. Wait.
- My hair.

51:13.653 --> 51:15.071
I'm sorry.

51:15.155 --> 51:16.323
Are you okay?

51:16.406 --> 51:19.159
- That stings.
- It must hurt a lot. I'm so sorry.

51:20.786 --> 51:22.662
What?

51:30.796 --> 51:31.838
Oh, no. I'm sorry.

51:31.922 --> 51:34.299
Oh, no. I'm so sorry.

51:34.925 --> 51:36.468
Oh, no.

51:52.067 --> 51:53.360
I'm an idiot, right?

51:54.277 --> 51:55.946
Yes. You are.

51:56.029 --> 51:58.573
I thought long and hard,

51:58.657 --> 52:01.326
but I really didn't know how to react.

52:03.620 --> 52:06.414
I really wasn't prepared for it.

52:13.380 --> 52:15.382
I can't believe him.

52:15.465 --> 52:17.843
The first thing he said was…

52:18.426 --> 52:19.553
Hold on.

52:20.387 --> 52:23.265
But we weren't planning to have a baby.

52:24.891 --> 52:26.393
Aren't you dumbfounded?

52:27.811 --> 52:29.396
What did you expect him to say?

52:30.272 --> 52:33.900
I expected him to at least say,
"I'm really happy."

52:33.984 --> 52:35.735
"Is the baby healthy?"

52:35.819 --> 52:37.487
"Congratulations."

52:37.571 --> 52:38.989
He could have said many things.

52:45.203 --> 52:47.789
What? What is it?

52:49.958 --> 52:52.919
You must really love him.

52:56.339 --> 52:57.799
I thought he'd be much more mature.

52:57.883 --> 53:00.927
But he turned out to be a baby
once we got married.

53:01.011 --> 53:02.846
He's still a bit immature.

53:04.472 --> 53:07.475
I married him
because I thought I could rely on him,

53:07.559 --> 53:08.852
but I was wrong.

53:09.394 --> 53:11.855
I thought he'd be on my side,

53:13.148 --> 53:14.941
but we kept disagreeing.

53:18.278 --> 53:20.196
No relationship is easy.

53:20.780 --> 53:22.115
Even with your parents.

53:22.198 --> 53:23.867
I've never been comfortable

53:24.534 --> 53:26.620
in my relationship with my father.

53:28.455 --> 53:31.833
Parents, children, spouses, siblings…

53:31.917 --> 53:33.752
It's more difficult and exhausting

53:34.544 --> 53:35.712
since they're family.

53:35.795 --> 53:37.589
That's why you become more upset

53:38.882 --> 53:40.133
and hurt.

53:43.762 --> 53:45.722
I'm glad I decided…

53:47.474 --> 53:49.142
to never get married.

53:51.353 --> 53:52.562
Don't you think so?

53:53.855 --> 53:56.608
What's wrong? Are things
not working out with Director Jin?

54:00.403 --> 54:02.489
We broke up.

54:07.953 --> 54:10.830
There's still time until the baby is born,

54:10.914 --> 54:12.540
so take your time preparing.

54:12.624 --> 54:14.626
Raising a baby is expensive.

54:15.418 --> 54:18.630
We're barely paying rent
and making ends meet.

54:19.839 --> 54:21.967
I'm still not giving you half,
so don't bring it up again.

54:22.050 --> 54:24.469
I heard English kindergartens
are really pricey.

54:25.804 --> 54:27.806
You even thought of that?

54:27.889 --> 54:30.725
Learning English at a young age
is crucial these days.

54:30.809 --> 54:32.185
I can't give up on that.

54:37.649 --> 54:39.275
You're actually happy, right?

54:42.320 --> 54:44.030
To be honest…

54:46.032 --> 54:48.785
I'm worried that I won't be

54:50.036 --> 54:51.454
a good dad.

54:52.455 --> 54:55.709
I'm already struggling
to be a good husband.

55:00.296 --> 55:01.256
You'll do well.

55:05.510 --> 55:06.678
You will.

55:08.304 --> 55:11.683
You've always done your best
when it came to your responsibilities.

55:11.766 --> 55:15.061
It was just that I was
a lousy and fussy perfectionist.

55:19.983 --> 55:22.652
Are you really going
to end things with Si-woo?

55:29.659 --> 55:31.202
Hey, Ha-kyung.

55:34.581 --> 55:37.250
You can't maintain
a relationship if it's one-sided.

55:37.751 --> 55:40.211
Exactly why does he want to break up?

55:41.504 --> 55:42.630
I'm not sure.

55:43.339 --> 55:45.008
There were many reasons,

55:45.091 --> 55:46.259
but it's obvious.

55:47.343 --> 55:48.803
I'm just not good enough for him.

55:49.387 --> 55:52.640
Hey, don't be ridiculous.
You're a terrific woman.

55:53.224 --> 55:54.225
Okay?

55:54.309 --> 55:55.894
You're smart, competent,

55:55.977 --> 55:58.188
responsible, and athletic.

55:58.271 --> 56:01.066
Do you still not know
how charming you are?

56:02.776 --> 56:05.070
- You dumped me too.
- What?

56:09.574 --> 56:11.326
That was because…

56:11.409 --> 56:13.328
Forget it. That's water under the bridge.

56:15.455 --> 56:17.707
Getting dumped like that twice means

56:18.291 --> 56:20.502
I'm not suited to date anyone.

56:21.086 --> 56:22.128
Come on.

56:23.171 --> 56:24.756
So treat your wife well.

56:24.839 --> 56:26.382
Stop drinking.

56:26.466 --> 56:29.803
Buy some flowers or a gift
at the department store before it closes.

56:30.553 --> 56:31.387
Bye.

56:32.680 --> 56:34.307
I was the lousy one.

56:35.517 --> 56:37.560
It wasn't because of you.

56:39.979 --> 56:42.524
You're a good person, Ha-kyung.

56:48.029 --> 56:49.155
Bye.

57:12.428 --> 57:14.013
LEE SI-WOO'S FATHER

57:20.228 --> 57:21.396
Hello?

57:22.188 --> 57:23.731
I was never happy

57:24.399 --> 57:27.235
to be his son.

57:27.902 --> 57:29.404
It wasn't my fault.

57:30.155 --> 57:31.656
But my parents…

57:34.117 --> 57:35.660
blamed me

57:35.743 --> 57:38.079
for being born into this world.

57:39.622 --> 57:41.040
"It's your fault."

57:43.710 --> 57:45.628
"You're the reason why

57:47.046 --> 57:49.132
your mother sacrificed her life."

57:49.966 --> 57:52.427
Then she passed away
at an early age due to illness.

57:53.595 --> 57:56.890
My father even blamed her death on me.

57:59.726 --> 58:00.935
"You're the reason why

58:02.145 --> 58:04.105
your mother died early."

58:04.772 --> 58:06.107
How harsh of him.

58:07.859 --> 58:10.236
They shouldn't have had me
if they weren't confident.

58:11.321 --> 58:12.989
Parents who give birth

58:13.072 --> 58:16.493
and blame everything on their child…

58:18.995 --> 58:20.830
are the worst.

58:39.432 --> 58:40.642
Hey, Honey.

58:41.309 --> 58:42.185
I'm sorry.

58:44.729 --> 58:48.358
My mom's condition
is worse than I thought.

58:49.234 --> 58:51.778
Yes. We're on our way home.

58:53.571 --> 58:56.908
Honey, the bus is here.
I'll call you back later.

59:03.414 --> 59:05.083
Sir, please give me a minute.

59:06.834 --> 59:08.211
Let me help.

59:08.294 --> 59:10.630
Okay. Thank you.

59:15.552 --> 59:17.136
- Go ahead.
- Thank you.

59:22.183 --> 59:25.311
Don't cry, Se-chan. It's okay.

59:30.608 --> 59:31.776
I'm sorry.

59:35.321 --> 59:37.699
Goodness. My baby.

59:39.242 --> 59:42.829
Taking a leave for childbirth
and childrearing will mean

59:42.912 --> 59:45.331
she won't be working for a year or two.

59:45.915 --> 59:47.458
Once that happens,

59:47.542 --> 59:50.044
she will lose her edge.

59:50.128 --> 59:53.423
If she can't get on top of her game,
she'll eventually lose her job.

59:54.674 --> 59:56.259
It's okay.

59:58.094 --> 01:00:00.013
Don't cry.

01:00:08.771 --> 01:00:09.939
Hi.

01:00:11.107 --> 01:00:13.234
You must be exhausted. Give me that.

01:00:14.652 --> 01:00:15.737
What's all this?

01:00:21.159 --> 01:00:23.536
I couldn't even congratulate you.

01:00:23.620 --> 01:00:25.121
I'm sorry.

01:00:25.663 --> 01:00:27.624
I wasn't meaning to do that.

01:00:28.708 --> 01:00:30.418
It was just so sudden.

01:00:34.839 --> 01:00:36.591
It must have been hard
to keep it to yourself.

01:00:36.674 --> 01:00:38.259
I'm so thankful

01:00:38.843 --> 01:00:40.470
and I love you so much, Yu-jin.

01:00:50.104 --> 01:00:52.482
I booked an appointment
with my ob-gyn next week.

01:00:54.859 --> 01:00:55.860
Really?

01:00:56.444 --> 01:00:57.737
What day?

01:00:57.820 --> 01:00:59.906
Let me come with you. I'll make time.

01:01:03.034 --> 01:01:05.370
I don't think it's right to have a baby

01:01:06.371 --> 01:01:08.539
when we're not prepared.

01:01:13.044 --> 01:01:14.545
What are you saying?

01:01:15.588 --> 01:01:17.423
Let's be frank. You don't want it either.

01:01:18.132 --> 01:01:20.843
A baby in our current situation?

01:01:21.803 --> 01:01:23.137
It's too much of a burden.

01:01:24.472 --> 01:01:27.600
Yu-jin, are you going to…

01:01:28.976 --> 01:01:30.311
Let's do that.

01:01:30.395 --> 01:01:31.521
Okay?

01:02:10.101 --> 01:02:11.644
Happiness…

01:02:13.104 --> 01:02:15.064
isn't a given in life.

01:02:16.190 --> 01:02:18.067
That's why we broke up.

01:02:18.151 --> 01:02:19.861
I could see

01:02:20.695 --> 01:02:23.406
that we'd never be happy
no matter how hard we tried.

01:02:25.241 --> 01:02:26.075
I didn't want her

01:02:27.618 --> 01:02:29.787
to carry my burdens.

01:02:31.664 --> 01:02:32.790
That's why.

01:02:49.098 --> 01:02:50.975
Hello, ma'am.

01:02:53.019 --> 01:02:56.939
- I was just passing by.
- Where is Ha-kyung?

01:02:57.023 --> 01:02:58.107
Sorry?

01:02:58.191 --> 01:03:00.276
Where is my daughter?

01:03:09.035 --> 01:03:11.245
I'm here to see Mr. Lee Myung-han.

01:03:11.329 --> 01:03:12.872
Okay. One minute, please.

01:03:12.955 --> 01:03:15.500
Oh, are you his guardian?

01:03:18.044 --> 01:03:18.920
Well, yes.

01:03:19.921 --> 01:03:21.756
He was in a car accident.

01:03:22.256 --> 01:03:25.218
After doing a blood test
and a few other checkups,

01:03:25.301 --> 01:03:26.844
I found something strange.

01:03:27.595 --> 01:03:29.597
- Something strange?
- Yes.

01:03:34.769 --> 01:03:36.479
LEE SI-WOO

01:03:45.655 --> 01:03:47.281
Can you please pick up?

01:04:02.463 --> 01:04:03.548
You.

01:04:04.632 --> 01:04:06.050
Yes, ma'am.

01:04:06.133 --> 01:04:07.593
Let's talk.

01:04:09.136 --> 01:04:10.221
Sure.

01:04:11.681 --> 01:04:14.934
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

01:04:15.017 --> 01:04:16.435
LEE SI-WOO

01:04:24.485 --> 01:04:28.030
Amid the clear, fall weather
throughout the country,

01:04:28.114 --> 01:04:30.658
a sudden cold wave advisory

01:04:30.741 --> 01:04:32.785
has been announced.

01:04:32.869 --> 01:04:34.453
This sudden freezing weather

01:04:34.537 --> 01:04:36.956
could easily alarm our bodies.

01:04:37.039 --> 01:04:39.750
At times like this,
it's important that you

01:04:39.834 --> 01:04:41.752
take care of your immune system.

01:05:31.010 --> 01:05:32.887
So when do you think
this cold will subside?

01:05:32.970 --> 01:05:34.013
As things stand…

01:05:34.096 --> 01:05:36.349
We may have to overturn the forecast.

01:05:36.432 --> 01:05:38.476
You're going to take the bullet
for what Si-woo said?

01:05:38.559 --> 01:05:40.102
Say that again!

01:05:40.186 --> 01:05:41.437
What are you doing?

01:05:42.438 --> 01:05:43.814
Did you already know?

01:05:43.898 --> 01:05:45.232
You need a biopsy.

01:05:45.316 --> 01:05:47.234
My relationships started with love

01:05:47.318 --> 01:05:50.029
but my father was always
at the end of them.

01:05:50.112 --> 01:05:51.614
Because you'll regret it.

01:05:51.697 --> 01:05:54.367
You might regret it later.

01:05:54.450 --> 01:05:57.328
I still like you a lot.

01:05:57.912 --> 01:05:58.955
Do you know that?

01:05:59.705 --> 01:06:04.502
Subtitle translation by: Soo-ji Kim
